btw I use something like that for logger so it may be called from another thread

```
        StreamHandler handler = new StreamHandler() {

            @Override
            public void publish(LogRecord record) {
                if (channel != null) {
                    String record0 = getFormatter().format(record);
                    channel.write(new TextWebSocketFrame(record0));
                }
            }
        };
```

I think what maybe happening is the server is sending the text frame immediately after the handshake.  This does not give time for the client to add the `WebSocket08FrameEncoder` to the pipeline so  the text frame is being processed as a HTTP Message.

The following is from `WebSocketClientHandshaker08`.  I think the packet may have been received by the client prior to the future completing.

```
    ChannelFuture future = channel.write(request);
    future.addListener(new ChannelFutureListener() {
        @Override
        public void operationComplete(ChannelFuture future) {
            ChannelPipeline p = future.channel().pipeline();
            p.addAfter(
                    p.context(HttpRequestEncoder.class).name(),
                    "ws-encoder", new WebSocket08FrameEncoder(true));

            if (future.isSuccess()) {
                handshakeFuture.setSuccess();
            } else {
                handshakeFuture.setFailure(future.cause());
            }
        }
    });
```

Actual I think it is a bug in ReplayingDecoder... Let me do more testing

Sent from my iPhone. Excuse any typos....

